<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sándor Garbai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sándor Garbai was a Hungarian Social Democratic politician who chaired the Revolutionary Governing Council of the Hungarian Soviet Republic in 1919. Formally head of the government, he had less real power than <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bela-kun">Béla Kun</a>, who controlled foreign affairs. After the republic fell in August 1919 he went into exile, living in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sandor-garbai.jpg" alt="Sándor Garbai" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pál M. Vajda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garbai_S%C3%A1ndor_(retouched).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
